meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    producer: United Nations
    title: Estimates and projections of women of reproductive age who are married or in a union
    description: |-
      This dataset gives estimates and projections of the share and number of women aged 15 to 49 who are married or in a union, from 1970 to 2050. It covers 225 countries and areas, as well as world regions and groups of countries by income and level of development. The data is also broken down into five-year age groups.

      A union means living with a partner in the same household, whether married or not.

      The estimates combine census and survey data on the share of women who are married or in a union with estimates of the number of women in each age group from World Population Prospects 2024. The survey data comes from the World Marriage Data 2019 database, complemented by more recent surveys, such as the Demographic and Health Surveys and the Multiple Indicator Cluster Surveys.

      For each country, values up to its most recent census or survey are estimates, and values after it are projections.
    # NOTE: The UN names this release by edition ("2024"), so the citation year stays 2024 while date_published is the
    #  date of the file we download. The UN replaced the original 2024 file (..._fp_rev-2024.xlsx, August 2024) with a
    #  revised one (..._fp_rev-2024_rev.xlsx, April 2025) without announcing it; the only change was the addition of
    #  Guadeloupe. The url_main page still links the original file; the revised one is linked from
    #  https://www.un.org/development/desa/pd/data/family-planning-data. Check both pages for a newer edition next time.
    date_published: "2025-04-22"

    # Citation
    citation_full: |-
      United Nations, Department of Economic and Social Affairs, Population Division (2024). Estimates and Projections of Women of Reproductive Age Who Are Married or in a Union 2024. New York: United Nations.
    attribution_short: UN

    # Files
    url_main: https://www.un.org/development/desa/pd/content/family-planning-0
    url_download: https://www.un.org/development/desa/pd/sites/www.un.org.development.desa.pd/files/undesa_pd_ds_1970-2030_fp_rev-2024_rev.xlsx
    date_accessed: 2026-10-15

